<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chernorizets Hrabar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 900</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Hrabar the Monk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chernorizets Hrabar was a Bulgarian monk and writer of the late 9th or early 10th century, associated with the literary circle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a>. His treatise On the Letters defends the Slavonic alphabet created by Cyril against those who held that only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a>, Greek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> were fit for Scripture. Nothing certain is known of his life, and the name, meaning 'Hrabar the Monk', may be a pseudonym.</p></div>
